## Check for hidden content first

The earlier `ls` doesn't show old object versions or recently deleted objects:
```bash
gcloud storage ls -a -r gs://pg-ae-n-app-125609-logs-116609
```
Empty output means there are no objects and no versions. Objects deleted in the last 7 days would still be recoverable, because the bucket has a 7-day soft delete.

## Options

| | What happens | Risk |
|---|---|---|
| **A. Ask the project provisioning team** | Nothing changes until they answer | none |
| **B. Delete it** | The `US` resource is gone | Irreversible. If an org process created it, it may be recreated in `US`. |
| **C. Leave it and document it** | Nothing changes | The residency rule is not met |

**Recommendation: A.** Bucket location can't be changed in place, so the fix is a new regional bucket plus deleting this one, and the owner must agree.

